From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shikosu <teovidal01@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 17:41:50 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] aot: jump tables resolved at translation time; translation
 cache; blocker 2

jump_tables.py reads the switch tables (LLVM byte/halfword, GCC signed byte with an extended add, word
relative) by a symbolic run before each br; each case becomes an entry lifted from its own address with the
whole function around it (remill-lift --entry_address). A GCC switch that cost 20 JIT entries costs none; 78
real functions with switches equal Unicorn over 1,152 cases. Aot(cache=...) keeps lifted and compiled
functions and the finished library under a hash of bytes, address and toolchain: a second build of 2,012
functions takes 0.2 s instead of 19 s. elf_module.py build warms it.

Upstream-Status: pending
Reason: jump tables and the translation cache of the AArch64 -> x86_64 recompilation (NX2Linux); no game data in the tests
Issue: none yet (NX2Linux, branch feat/teo-t7-module-reel)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
